# API Reference

This page is the entry point for the sibl library API. sibl is a Zig package. You import it with `@import("sibl")`. The root module re-exports every public type and function from `src/root.zig`.

## How to import sibl

Add sibl as a dependency in your `build.zig.zon`, then import the module:

```zig
const sibl = @import("sibl");
```

All public types are available on this namespace. For example:

```zig
var table = sibl.SymbolTable.init(allocator);
defer table.deinit();

var layout = sibl.Layout.init(allocator, 0x400000, 4096);
defer layout.deinit();
```

## Modules

| Module | What it does | Page |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `alloc` | Arena allocator and scratch buffer | [alloc](/docs/api-alloc) |
| `args` | CLI flag parsing and options | [args](/docs/api-args) |
| `target` | Target detection and page size | [target](/docs/api-target) |
| `file` | Memory-mapped file reader | [file](/docs/api-file) |
| `elf` | ELF parsing | [elf](/docs/api-elf) |
| `strtab` | String table reader and builder | [strtab](/docs/api-strtab) |
| `coff` | PE and COFF parsing | [coff](/docs/api-coff) |
| `macho` | Mach-O parsing | [macho](/docs/api-macho) |
| `archive` | Static archive parsing | [archive](/docs/api-archive) |
| `symbol` | Global symbol table | [symbol](/docs/api-symbol) |
| `layout` | Section grouping and address layout | [layout](/docs/api-layout) |
| `reloc` | Relocation engine | [reloc](/docs/api-reloc) |
| `entry` | Entry point resolution | [entry](/docs/api-entry) |
| `rules` | Section placement rules | [rules](/docs/api-rules) |
| `defsym` | `--defsym` symbol assignment | [defsym](/docs/api-defsym) |
| `templates` | Default layout templates | [templates](/docs/api-templates) |

## Common flow

A typical link pass uses these steps:

1. Parse arguments with `sibl.parseArgs`.
2. Detect the target with `sibl.TargetInfo.detect`.
3. Open input files with `sibl.MappedFile.open`.
4. Parse each file with `elf`, `coff`, `macho`, or `archive`.
5. Add symbols to a `sibl.SymbolTable`.
6. Add sections to a `sibl.Layout`.
7. Apply placement rules, `--defsym`, and a template.
8. Call `layout.computeAddresses`, `layout.buildSegments`, and `layout.accountSizes`.
9. Resolve the entry point with `sibl.resolveEntry`.
10. Apply relocations with `sibl.applyReloc` or `sibl.resolveAndApplyRelocs`.

## Error handling

Most functions return an error union. sibl uses Zig error sets. You can use `try` and let the error move up, or handle it with a `switch`. The main executable shows this pattern.

## Memory management

sibl uses explicit allocators. The `LinkerAllocators` type wraps an arena for bulk data and a base allocator for structures that need manual resizing. Call `deinit` on `LinkerAllocators`, `Options`, `Layout`, `SymbolTable`, `MappedFile`, and output sections when you are done.
